By the divisibility rule for 3, a number is divisible by 3 iff its digit sum is divisible by 3. The digits 1 through 5 sum to 15, which is divisible by 3, so any 4-digit number formed by omitting one digit will be divisible by 3 exactly when the omitted digit is itself divisible by 3. Among {1,2,3,4,5}, the only such digit is 3.

Thus we must use the digits {1,2,4,5}. To maximize the number, place the largest digits in the most significant positions: 5, then 4, then 2, then 1, giving 5421.

\boxed{5421}
